    <string name="strava_title">Upload to Strava</string>
    <string name="strava_intro">Strava accepts the FIT file from RideComp. Upload is free and manual:</string>
    <string name="strava_step_1">1. Open the ride in RideComp and tap EXPORT FIT. Choose Strava if it is offered, or save the file (Drive or Downloads).</string>
    <string name="strava_step_2">2. In a browser go to strava.com, sign in, and open “Upload activity” (on a phone, switch the browser to “Desktop site” if the page is missing).</string>
    <string name="strava_step_3">3. Choose “File”, select the .fit file and save. Speed, distance, elevation and (from Phase 2) heart rate, cadence and power appear in Strava.</string>
    <string name="strava_note">Automatic upload via the Strava API is an optional later feature and needs a Strava subscription.</string>
    <string name="strava_open">OPEN STRAVA UPLOAD PAGE</string>
